. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         *We meisure leisure as hours spent on physical activity and hobbies (
> based on variables pli0051 and pli0162). 
.         *Our measure of gender equaliy (GEoutcome) is the absolute value of t
> he difference between the man and the woman in leisure time. 
.         *Key idea - having similar amount of hours for leisure is a proxy for
>  gender equality. 
. 
.         *To test if having a daugher increases gender equality, we estimate a
> n OLS regression with GEoutcome as dependent variable. 
.         *The main independent variable of interest is d_daughters which is 1 
> if the person has at least one 
.         *d_daughter and 0 if the person has only sons (missing if no children
> ). We include other control variables.
. 
.         *Note that this analysis differs from the pre-analysis plan. The outc
> ome is different. 
. 
.         reg GEoutcome d_daughter age kid1age male germborn i.edu i.syear if s
> ex!=parsex,cluster (hid)

